% An error made silent (docs/plans/plan_bug_analyses.md, A3): mini-analyze
% -bugs, over exceptions.dl's arrives and the facts of Closure_facts
% (FACTS.md):
%   silent(T, E)       a case of the try T catches E, its answer a constant
%   silent_all(T)      ... catches all (_, a variable), its answer a constant
% and says
%   swallowed(T, E)    the error E may arrive at T, from its body, and a
%                      case answers a constant: nothing said, the caller
%                      not told
%
%     let code = try f () with _ -> 1 in              (c5086383^, Process.ml)
%
% rc's forked child: a pipe's open that failed, a Sys_error, ended it in
% silence (exit 1, no word), and a fork's Unix_error the same (7f7ce094).
% And
%
%     let set name v = try put ... v with Unix_error _ -> ()   (4f00134c^)
%
% a variable /env could not hold left out, the program started without
% it: a mkfile's recipe with an empty list.
%
% design:
% A grep for "with _ -> ()" finds some 970 lines in ix: most stop a loop
% (End_of_file), say a value is not there (Not_found -> None), or try a
% conversion (int_of_string's Failure). What is reported is a case that
% says nothing over what may arrive and is an error of the system: the
% join with arrives is what grep cannot do, a with _ -> () around code
% that raises only End_of_file not reported. error(E) is the list; a
% program's own exception is not in it (its catches are its design, as
% Exit). An earlier case that catches E and says something is seen
% (catches, without silent); its guard is not (a case with a guard
% catches nothing for sure, so silent_all after it is reported).
%
% others:
% Java's "catch (Exception e) {}" is a classic of its linters (PMD's
% EmptyCatchBlock, Error Prone's), by the tree alone. Weimer and Necula
% ("Finding and preventing run-time error handling mistakes", OOPSLA
% 2004) followed what may be thrown, as here.

error('Unix.Unix_error').
error(caml_exn_Sys_error).

% What fails and is told by what comes next or does not matter, measured
% on ix's 44 programs (plan_bug_analyses.md, A3): a close or a remove,
% best effort, the end of a process or of a file not needed; an exec,
% which comes back only when it failed, the next line saying so
% ((try execv ... with _ -> ()); prerr_endline "can't exec").
release('Unix.close').
release('Unix.closedir').
release('Unix.unlink').
release('Unix.rmdir').
release('Unix.kill').
release('CapUnix.kill').
release('FS.remove_any').
release(sys_remove).
release('Unix.execv').
release('Unix.execve').
release('Unix.execvp').
release('CapUnix.execv').
release('CapUnix.execve').
released(G) :- release(G).
released(G) :- curried(G, F), released(F).
quiet(S) :- callee(S, _, _, G, _, _), released(G).
quiet(S) :- primitive(S, P), release(P).

% E may come to T from its body: raised or called there, by what is not
% quiet, or through a try in it
cause(T, E) :- at(S, _, _, E), in_try(S, T), \+ quiet(S).
cause(T2, E) :- passes(T, _, _, E), try_in_try(T, T2).

swallowed(T, E) :- silent(T, E), cause(T, E), error(E).
swallowed(T, E) :- silent_all(T), cause(T, E), error(E), \+ catches(T, E).
